WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:04.901
WE WILL DO ON THE SHOW TONIGHT

00:00:04.902 --> 00:00:06.703
IS WHAT WE WILL ONLY SHOW YOU

00:00:06.704 --> 00:00:07.537
HERE.

00:00:07.538 --> 00:00:09.238
WE HAVE SPENT THE PAST TWO DAYS

00:00:09.239 --> 00:00:11.174
WITH THE BORDER PATROL ON THE

00:00:11.175 --> 00:00:12.842
GROUND.

00:00:12.843 --> 00:00:13.309
AND IN THE AIR.

00:00:13.310 --> 00:00:13.810
AND ON THE WATER.

00:00:13.811 --> 00:00:15.411
AND YOU WILL BE SHOCKED BY SOME

00:00:15.412 --> 00:00:16.345
OF WHAT THE BORDER PATROL SHOWED

00:00:16.346 --> 00:00:16.612
US.

00:00:16.613 --> 00:00:20.116
HERE IS JUST A LITTLE OF WHAT WE

00:00:20.117 --> 00:00:25.288
WERE ABLE TO SEE FOR OURSELVES.

00:00:25.289 --> 00:00:27.323
&gt;&gt; MOST OF THE TIME YOU CAN WALK

00:00:27.324 --> 00:00:31.527
ACROSS THE RIVER.

00:00:31.528 --> 00:00:33.763
BUT AGAIN, THAT IS WHERE IT IS

00:00:33.764 --> 00:00:34.764
POTENTIALLY DANGEROUS.

00:00:34.765 --> 00:00:37.600
I CAN WALK ON THIS AND SUDDENLY,

00:00:37.601 --> 00:00:38.634
REACHES OVER THEIR HEAD.

00:00:38.635 --> 00:00:40.903
THE CURRENT IS STRONG AND THEY

00:00:40.904 --> 00:00:42.972
GET SWEPT AWAY.

00:00:42.973 --> 00:00:46.209
YOU TRY TO HOLD A BABY ABOVE HER

00:00:46.210 --> 00:00:47.110
HEAD TO COMAY'S SMALL CHILDREN

00:00:47.111 --> 00:00:48.044
ABOVE THEIR HEAD.

00:00:48.045 --> 00:00:50.580
YOU WILL SEE THE MOTHER IS

00:00:50.581 --> 00:00:51.314
TRYING TO STRUGGLE HERSELF AS

00:00:51.315 --> 00:00:53.149
SHE FIGHTS THE CURRENT TO KEEP

00:00:53.150 --> 00:00:55.151
THE CHILD ABOVE HEAD AND THEY

00:00:55.152 --> 00:00:55.685
BOTH CAN'T MAKE IT.

00:00:55.686 --> 00:00:57.887
IF YOU ARE LUCKY YOU GO BACK TO

00:00:57.888 --> 00:01:01.991
THEIR LAND AND WAIT FOR HELP.

00:01:01.992 --> 00:01:04.494
&gt;&gt; YOU CAN SEE RIGHT ON THE

00:01:04.495 --> 00:01:09.298
BANKS, THE TEAM TO SEE THE TRASH

00:01:09.299 --> 00:01:11.434
BAGS, AND THOSE TRASH BAGS TO

00:01:11.435 --> 00:01:13.269
KEEP THEIR CLOSE DRIVE.

00:01:13.270 --> 00:01:14.737
YOU ALSO USE TRASH BAGS WHEN

00:01:14.738 --> 00:01:19.308
THEY COME ACROSS.

00:01:19.309 --> 00:01:23.813
&gt;&gt; SO THIS IS A LANDING AREA.

00:01:23.814 --> 00:01:24.981
WE WENT THAT EASY ACCESS TO THE

00:01:24.982 --> 00:01:25.648
COUNTRY.

00:01:25.649 --> 00:01:29.952
&gt;&gt; THEY GIVE THEM THAT -- THEY

00:01:29.953 --> 00:01:33.756
HAVE TO SLOW DOWN TO GET WATER

00:01:33.757 --> 00:01:35.458
AGENTS MORE PROTECTED.

00:01:35.459 --> 00:01:40.630
AND WE RESPOND.

00:01:40.631 --> 00:01:44.667
SO THESE FOUR UPRIVER.

00:01:44.668 --> 00:01:46.636
INTO THE BOAT CAN YOU HAVE TO GO

00:01:46.637 --> 00:01:48.805
UP THERE AND RESCUED THEM AS YOU

00:01:48.806 --> 00:01:49.172
CAN TELL.

00:01:49.173 --> 00:01:52.542
THEY ARE ALL SOAKING WET.

00:01:52.543 --> 00:01:56.779
THAT LITTLE TUBE.

00:01:56.780 --> 00:01:59.115
THESE TWO WERE RESCUED BY THE

00:01:59.116 --> 00:02:03.519
BOAT.

00:02:03.520 --> 00:02:06.122
&gt;&gt; FOUR PEOPLE DROWNED THE OTHER

00:02:06.123 --> 00:02:07.456
DAY, SAME CIRCUMSTANCES.

00:02:07.457 --> 00:02:08.424
&gt;&gt; Laura: HOW DO THEY KNOW

00:02:08.425 --> 00:02:12.628
WHERE TO CROSS?

00:02:12.629 --> 00:02:25.107
&gt;&gt; [SPEAKING IN NATIVE TONGUE]

00:02:25.108 --> 00:02:28.978
&gt;&gt; YOU CAN SEE WE HAVE EVERY

00:02:28.979 --> 00:02:31.280
SIDE IMAGINABLE.

00:02:31.281 --> 00:02:34.083
DIAPERS, FORMULA, JUICES,

00:02:34.084 --> 00:02:36.719
SNACKS, MEALS.

00:02:36.720 --> 00:02:37.220
WE PARTNER UP WITH

00:02:37.221 --> 00:02:38.721
NONGOVERNMENTAL AGENCIES AND

00:02:38.722 --> 00:02:39.755
THEY WILL HELP DONATE SOME

00:02:39.756 --> 00:02:41.123
CLOSING TO MY CLOTHING.

00:02:41.124 --> 00:02:42.925
A LOT OF THIS HAS BROUGHT HIM BY

00:02:42.926 --> 00:02:44.126
THE AGENTS THEMSELVES.

00:02:44.127 --> 00:02:45.094
WE ARE PARENTS AND SO MOST

00:02:45.095 --> 00:02:48.931
AGENTS HAVE THREE OR FOUR KIDS.

00:02:48.932 --> 00:02:51.667
AND THEY OUTGROW AND GIVE THEM

00:02:51.668 --> 00:02:54.003
HAND-ME-DOWNS.

00:02:54.004 --> 00:02:57.240
&gt;&gt; HERE WE ARE AT EAGLE PASS.

00:02:57.241 --> 00:03:03.246
EAGLE PASS SECTOR COME UP

00:03:03.247 --> 00:03:04.013
HUNDRED 40 MILES.

00:03:04.014 --> 00:03:05.147
AND THIS IS 2 MILES OF THE

00:03:05.148 --> 00:03:07.917
400 -- 4 MILES.

00:03:07.918 --> 00:03:09.619
WE WILL SHOW YOU WHERE IT IS AND

00:03:09.620 --> 00:03:11.854
WHERE IT ALL BEGINS BEHIND US.

00:03:11.855 --> 00:03:14.056
AND UP HERE IS WHERE IT ENDS.

00:03:14.057 --> 00:03:20.696
THAT IS THE END OF THE DASH &gt;&gt;

00:03:20.697 --> 00:03:21.998
HERE WE ARE IN THE DEL RIO

00:03:21.999 --> 00:03:26.169
SECTOR OF THE BORDER WITH THE

